'''Immunity''' is a stat that prevents and removes certain effects (e.g. [[debuff]]s or [[ailment]]s) or nullifies certain [[Receiving Damage|damage]] types. Immunity is typically worded as either {{c|mod|Immune to X}} or {{c|mod|Immunity to X}}.

__TOC__

==Mechanics==
The most common forms of immunity prevent [[ailment]]s, but items such as the {{il|Eye of Chayula}} can provide other immunities.

Note that this should not be confused with {{c|mod|Cannot be X}}; although similar, and often also referred to as immunity, this stat is more akin to [[avoidance]] and does not remove any existing effects.<ref>https://www.reddit.com/r/pathofexile/comments/av6k7b/comment/ehdolai/</ref>

It should also not be confused with {{c|mod|Unaffected by X}} or 100% effect reduction, which will cause the debuff icon to appear and affect the target, but have no actual effect. This is typically for situations where the debuff provides or enables a secondary beneficial effect.

===Damage immunity===
Damage immunity is a form of [[receiving damage|mitigation]]. It mitigates damage after [[damage taken as]], and damage mitigated by immunity counts as 'prevented' damage for e.g. {{psl|Untiring}} or {{psl|Divine Shield}}. Damage immunity will not prevent non-damage [[loss]] due to e.g. {{il|Dark Bargain}} or {{il|Rathpith Globe}}.

* A [[Shrine|Divine Shrine]] grants immunity to all damage.
* {{sl|id=ShadeForm}} and {{il|Null and Void}} grant temporary [[physical damage]] immunity.
* The [[Chaos Inoculation]] [[keystone]] grants [[chaos damage]] immunity.

The {{c|mod|Cannot take Reflected Physical/Elemental Damage}} modifiers are similar to damage immunity, though they apply both before ''and'' after [[damage taken as|damage shifts]].

==Monsters==
Some [[boss]]es are immune to certain ailments or effects such as [[stun]] or [[knockback]]. 

Some are immune to damage during certain phases of fights. [[Harbinger]]s are immune to direct damage and are instead defeated by slaying their summoned monsters. {{c|rare|Rare}} and {{c|unique|Unique}} monsters are immune to [[fleeing]].

==Pantheon==
===Major Gods===
* [[Soul of the Brine King]] grants {{c|mod|You cannot be Stunned if you've been Stunned or Blocked a Stunning Hit in the past 2 seconds}}
* [[Soul of the Brine King]] upgrade grants {{c|mod|Cannot be Frozen}}

===Minor Gods===
* [[Soul of Ralakesh]] upgrade grants {{c|mod|Cannot be Blinded}} and {{c|mod|You cannot be Maimed}}
* [[Soul of Abberath]] grants {{c|mod|Unaffected by Burning Ground}}

==Items==
===Modifiers===
[[Flask]]s can grant temporary immunity to [[bleeding]], [[curse]]s, [[poison]], [[ignite]], [[chill]], [[freeze]], and [[shock]] with the following suffix mods. These mods also remove the effect.
{{modifier table
|q_tables=mod_stats, spawn_weights
|q_join=mods._pageID=mod_stats._pageID, mods._pageID=spawn_weights._pageID
|q_where=
  (mod_stats.id LIKE "%immun%" OR mod_stats.id LIKE "%cannot_be%") AND domain=2 AND spawn_weights.weight >= 0
|stat_text=1
|spawn_weights=1
|level=1
|generation_type=1
|domain=1
}}

====Miscellaneous====
The {{il|Essence of Delirium}} grants immunity to [[poison]] when applied to [[boots]].

[[Jewel]]s can be [[corrupted]] to have {{c|mod|You cannot be cursed with Silence}}, {{c|mod|Corrupted Blood cannot be inflicted on you}}, {{c|mod|You cannot be hindered}}, or {{c|mod|You cannot be maimed}}.

